WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.790
A neural stem cell has two jobs.

2
00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:08.860
Stay a stem cell, and make cells that differentiate.

3
00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:11.580
Asymmetric division lets it do both.

4
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:15.300
In the fly, a neural stem cell is called a neuroblast.

5
00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:19.300
In most neuroblasts, the large daughter stays a stem cell.

6
00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:22.460
The small daughter is a ganglion mother cell.

7
00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:25.820
It divides once more to make two neurons or glia.

8
00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:31.080
This way, the neuroblast keeps making new cells without using up the stem cell.

9
00:00:32.033 --> 00:00:33.673
How does the cell sort the daughters?

10
00:00:34.633 --> 00:00:36.333
Polarity marks a top and a bottom.

11
00:00:37.353 --> 00:00:39.813
Par proteins and Inscuteable gather at the top.

12
00:00:40.713 --> 00:00:41.993
Inscuteable recruits Pins.

13
00:00:42.973 --> 00:00:47.573
Pins, with other proteins including Mud, lines the spindle up from top to bottom.

14
00:00:48.433 --> 00:00:50.973
The protein aPKC keeps Numb off the top.

15
00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:54.253
Numb, Prospero and Brat end up at the bottom.

16
00:00:55.393 --> 00:00:57.493
Division hands this cargo to the small daughter.

17
00:00:58.373 --> 00:01:03.073
There, Prospero enters the nucleus and shuts down genes for self-renewal and

18
00:01:03.073 --> 00:01:04.073
division.

19
00:01:04.417 --> 00:01:06.997
Numb shows how inherited cargo changes fate.

20
00:01:07.897 --> 00:01:09.237
Take the fly bristle precursor.

21
00:01:10.457 --> 00:01:13.277
Numb forms a crescent and passes to one daughter only.

22
00:01:14.197 --> 00:01:18.157
There it blocks Notch, a receptor that carries signals between touching cells.

23
00:01:19.057 --> 00:01:20.637
The sister can still hear Notch.

24
00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:25.360
The Numb daughter takes the inner branch, leading to the neuron and sheath.

25
00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:29.280
Its sister takes the outer branch, leading to the hair and socket.

26
00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:31.800
Here both branches differentiate.

27
00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:34.260
Notch chooses between their fates.

28
00:01:35.183 --> 00:01:36.443
Now test that rule.

29
00:01:37.623 --> 00:01:39.903
Remove Numb, and both daughters take the outer fate.

30
00:01:40.783 --> 00:01:44.403
The lineage makes four outer support cells and no neuron or sheath.

31
00:01:45.143 --> 00:01:48.123
Give Numb to both daughters, and both take the inner branch.

32
00:01:49.163 --> 00:01:51.323
Neurons and sheath cells form, but no bristle.

33
00:01:52.417 --> 00:01:56.037
Back in the fly brain, failed fate control can cause overgrowth.

34
00:01:56.897 --> 00:01:59.097
The daughter may keep behaving like a stem cell.

35
00:02:00.277 --> 00:02:01.877
Prospero and Brat guard different cells.

36
00:02:02.797 --> 00:02:06.097
Without Prospero, tumours arise from ganglion mother cells.

37
00:02:07.037 --> 00:02:11.717
Without Brat, they arise mainly from intermediate progenitors in type II lineages.

38
00:02:12.717 --> 00:02:17.597
These progenitors normally divide several times, each time making a ganglion mother

39
00:02:17.597 --> 00:02:18.597
cell.

40
00:02:18.917 --> 00:02:22.077
In mammals, the division plane predicts fate less reliably.

41
00:02:23.077 --> 00:02:24.117
The fly rule is clear.

42
00:02:25.117 --> 00:02:27.217
Polarity and spindle alignment sort the cargo.

43
00:02:28.177 --> 00:02:30.057
One daughter keeps the stem cell going.

44
00:02:30.877 --> 00:02:32.517
The other moves toward differentiation.
